NOT A HOW-TO
This is a research taxonomy + industry map, not a working L5 recipe.
Challenges named in the paper: unreliable feedback, update failure,
evaluator exploitation, and who still owns safety after autonomy rises.

CORE CLAIM
Current LLMs stall under scale. More tokens != unbounded intelligence.
The last human-built system is a seed. After that, the improver improves itself.

METRIC
HCI  Headroom-Closed Index
     0   = frontier of the entry year
     100 = saturated / perfect score
Shows remaining headroom is uneven:
     science high, software/tools/agents still open

TYPES / OBJECTS
Model            weights, architecture, training recipe
Improver         procedure that changes the model or harness
Evaluator        scorer / verifier of candidate updates
Experience       tasks, traces, deployment outcomes
Harness          tools, memory, prompts, workflow
Mechanism        the process that produces future improvements

VARIABLES (informal)
A_t              system state at step t
I_t              improver at step t
E_t              evaluator at step t
X_t              experience acquired at t
Delta            accepted persistent update
HCI(d)           remaining headroom in domain d

LOOP
observe limitation -> propose update -> verify -> persist -> reuse
If I_{t+1} = I_t(A_t, X_t) and I can rewrite I itself, that is L5.

AUTONOMY LADDER
B0   In-task only
     refine this answer, no persistent state
     Self-Refine style generate-feedback-refine

L1   Improvement-execution autonomy
     AI runs a human-designed improvement procedure
     fine-tune, filter data, apply labeled edits
     humans still define WHAT and HOW

L2   Improvement-strategy autonomy
     AI diagnoses weakness and chooses the intervention
     prompt search, agent/workflow search, training-code search
     humans still own the objective and search space

L3   Experience-acquisition autonomy
     AI decides what to practice next
     self-play, curricula, environment interaction
     learner state conditions future data

L4   Environment-adaptation autonomy
     deployment outcomes rewrite rules, tools, memory
     co-evolving evaluators, selective retention
     live world becomes part of the training loop

L5   Recursive meta-improvement
     AI redesigns the improver / evaluator / search itself
     methods humans may not have specified
     humans remain on mission, safety, acceptance only

FUNDAMENTALS
Persistent update     change must survive the episode
Closed loop           capability gain must feed the next gain
Attribution           did the system improve, or just search harder?
Verification          evaluator gaming is the failure mode
Safe inheritance      a bad update must not lock in

TRAJECTORY
human engineers  ->  seed system  ->  self-growing improver
linear gap       ->  vertical gap once L5 holds

